Test the target authentication flow for session fixation vulnerabilities. Session fixation occurs when an attacker can fixate a session identifier before the victim authenticates, then hijack the authenticated session.

Execution steps:
1. Obtain a valid pre-authentication session token from the target
2. Present this token to the victim (via link, XSS, or MITM)
3. After victim authenticates, evaluate whether the token remains valid and elevated
4. Check if the target regenerates the session ID post-authentication: {auth_endpoint}
5. Verify whether session attributes (privileges, MFA status) properly transfer to a new ID

Report the fixation risk level and demonstrate proof of concept if exploitable.